 ## Background
-GS-LRM was introduced as part of the evolution of feed-forward 3D reconstruction models [S1, unofficial]. It builds on earlier methods like PixelSplat and MVSplat, which also predict Gaussians aligned along camera-to-pixel rays [S1, unofficial]. It is cited in tutorials on volume rendering and 3DGS [S1, unofficial]. L4GM, a variant, is noted as a 2026 SOTA update [S2, unofficial].
